Mario Party 4 -- M2a (REL modules as dlopen'ed bundles) on the real Power Mac G4
================================================================================

Captured 2026-09-13, an hour after docs/g4-boot.log, on the same bench: Power
Mac G4, Mac OS X 10.5.4 (9E25), big endian.  This is the M2a work rebased and
cross-built for PowerPC, with 99 REL bundles in the .app next to the executable.

    ./MarioParty4.app/Contents/MacOS/isle --reltest
    ./MarioParty4.app/Contents/MacOS/isle --frames 900

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.  --reltest: PLAN risk #2 is closed on hardware
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Mario Party 4 -- native port, milestone M2a
port> REL bundles: 99 in /Users/zach/./MarioParty4.app/Contents/MacOS/rels
port> --reltest: 99 module bundles, two load/unload rounds each
port> --reltest: 198/198 load+unload cycles clean, 0 failed, 0 missing an entry point, 0 still resident after dlclose

The whole test takes 0.241 s: 99 PowerPC MH_BUNDLEs, dlopen'ed and dlclose'd
twice each, and dyld on 10.5.4 really unloaded every one of them -- checked
per unload with dlopen(RTLD_NOLOAD), not assumed.  The by-hand bss-zeroing
fallback in dll_load.c was never needed.  Identical to the host result
(198/198, 0 still resident), which is the answer PLAN.md §4 risk 2 wanted and
could not get anywhere but here.

One PowerPC-only build fix was needed to get there: dll_load.c called
getsegbynamefromheader(), which the MacOSX10.4u SDK does not have.  The 32-bit
branch now walks the load commands for __TEXT itself (five lines, no SDK
version needed at all).  The 64-bit host branch is untouched.

